WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.930
When an air liquid boundary moves across

00:00:03.930 --> 00:00:07.060
epithelial cells, mechanical forces can cause injury.

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:10.190
This question motivated a controlled laboratory model,

00:00:10.190 --> 00:00:12.426
not a trial in patients.

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:18.551
The published apparatus drives fluid over cells

00:00:18.551 --> 00:00:21.301
through a parallel plate flow chamber. Its

00:00:21.301 --> 00:00:24.052
components define the model, including the cover

00:00:24.052 --> 00:00:26.017
slips and the narrow channel.

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:34.051
A bubble advances across the monolayer, exposing

00:00:34.051 --> 00:00:37.301
cells to forces near the moving interface.

00:00:37.301 --> 00:00:40.552
Our animation explains the geometry without inventing

00:00:40.552 --> 00:00:41.945
numerical stress measurements.

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:48.590
The cell bearing cover slip sits beneath

00:00:48.590 --> 00:00:51.380
a gasket and a second cover slip.

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:54.170
Repeating that arrangement helps isolate exposure while

00:00:54.170 --> 00:00:56.561
limiting what the apparatus can represent.

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:03.697
The authors stained living and dead L2

00:01:03.697 --> 00:01:06.594
epithelial cells after the bubble moved over

00:01:06.594 --> 00:01:09.492
the layer. Their original micrographs compare a

00:01:09.492 --> 00:01:11.561
control with the experimental group.

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:19.065
The published cytoskeleton photographs show actin filaments

00:01:19.065 --> 00:01:22.330
in green and nuclei stained blue. Comparing

00:01:22.330 --> 00:01:25.595
control and bubble exposed cells adds structural

00:01:25.595 --> 00:01:27.927
context to the viability result.

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:33.738
A mechanical insult in a simplified system

00:01:33.738 --> 00:01:36.677
can change cell viability and organization. It

00:01:36.677 --> 00:01:39.616
does not by itself tell us how

00:01:39.616 --> 00:01:42.554
a patient's entire respiratory tract will respond.

00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:48.729
The chamber makes a hidden physical event

00:01:48.729 --> 00:01:51.657
experimentally accessible. Its strength is repeatability; its

00:01:51.657 --> 00:01:54.586
limit is the distance between a cell

00:01:54.586 --> 00:01:56.678
monolayer and the living lung.
